; per-level room tile-index maps (ROOMS_LANDSCAPE). Each level = 240 bytes (6 rooms x
; 8x5 tiles + spacing); draw_room reads ROOMS_LANDSCAPE + level*240 + room. Each DB row
; is one map row across the 6 rooms; LEVEL/ROOM annotations below.
;
; TILE CODE LEGEND (each code -> a 4x4 = 16-byte cell block in BACKGR_TILES):
;   $00       empty / sky (non-solid background)
;   $01       solid ground / floor (also $02 $03 $05 = floor variants)
;   $12       cannon        (do_cannon / find_room_tile look for $12)
;   $1B       rotator       (find_rotators - spawns aliens at ROTATORS)
;   $34       bridge        (find_bridge - animated by move_bridge)
;   $61       volcano vent  (find_volcanoes -> VOLCANO_1/VOLCANO_2)
;   others    decorative / structural scenery tiles (walls, ledges, pillars -
;             e.g. the $0A/$0B, $0C/$0D, $45/$46 vertical pairs); the
;             TILE_SET_1..4 groups are animated tiles (water/lava/etc).
; Deadliness (water/lava) is tested at the EXPANDED cell level, not here:
; check_drowning looks for cell value $EA (themes 0/1) / $ED (theme 3).
; The per-LEVEL tag comment (e.g. '2B 47 12 1B') lists that level's notable codes.
